apiVersion: 1

{# Grafana file-provisioned alerting — the contact point (#139).

   This is an Ansible TEMPLATE, not a static file under files/data/, because the
   destination address is a vault value and must not be committed. That has one
   consequence the role's tasks/main.yml has to handle and which must not be
   undone: the "Deploy Grafana provisioning" synchronize runs with delete:true
   over the same directory, so it carries
   `--exclude=alerting/contact-points.yaml`. Remove that exclude and the rsync
   deletes this file on every run, the template writes it back, and Grafana
   restarts on every deploy forever.

   Grafana does interpolate ${ENV} inside DATASOURCE provisioning files, which is
   how datasources.yaml gets its credentials. That is not documented for alerting
   provisioning, so this templates the value in rather than assuming.

   `addresses` below is vault_watchtower_email_to — the host's shared Gmail relay,
   see the comment block in templates/env.j2. Deliberately reusing watchtower's
   credentials rather than adding a second copy of the same Gmail app password to
   the vault. Keep every Jinja comment OUTSIDE the mapping below: a Jinja comment
   block sitting between `settings:` and its first key leaves the block's own
   indentation in the rendered output, which is valid YAML today only because
   `settings` has exactly one key. (And never write a literal comment-close
   sequence inside one of these blocks — it terminates the comment early and the
   rest of the prose renders into the file. Yes, that happened.) #}
contactPoints:
  - orgId: 1
    name: homelab-email
    receivers:
      - uid: homelab-email-primary
        type: email
        settings:
          addresses: {{ vault_watchtower_email_to }}
        disableResolveMessage: false
